From f44460bf5fe47c1cc3e9bd9c6f04d65424f219d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 00:55:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SCM export: NGFW extension of the config area + device
 inventory

- config types in groups identity / objects / network / policies / device (config-scope=), ~110 types from the
  pan.dev network / device / identity navigation: interfaces (ethernet, aggregate, L2 / L3 sub, loopback, tunnel,
  VLAN, DHCP), routing (logical routers, BGP profiles / route maps, route lists), DNS proxy, IKE / IPsec, QoS, SD-WAN
  profiles; NAT / PBF / QoS / SD-WAN rules (pre / post; qos-policy-rules moved to /config/network/v1); certificates
  and auth / server profiles per container; device settings and log match lists
- devices: /config/setup/v1/devices -> 03_devices.json + devices.csv (authcode redacted), device annotation in
  hierarchy.txt, manifest config.devices (connected, by model / folder, HA pairs), checklist items
- device folders: folder=<serial>, fallback device=<serial>; owner field device = folder
- Prisma Access folders: only objects / policies in the config area (network / identity via the PA areas)
- compare: devices by serial_number, folder assignment as assigned_folder (keep_owner), runtime fields ignored;
  scope aware side coverage
- sync: allow-network for the network / device groups, devices never written (SCM device management),
  device owner field kept
- manifest format_version 7; docs: README_pa_export, consultant guide (NGFW section), README_pa_compare / _sync,
  NEXT_STEPS verification

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SFP7DoEumroXLDgZkyZdE6
